{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stationary and time dependent thermal studies stationary and time dependent thermal studies","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","fileName":"Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Finite Element Thermal Modeling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Finite Element Thermal Modeling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stationary and time dependent thermal studies stationary and time dependent thermal studies","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","fileName":"Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies","heading":"Stationary and Time-Dependent Thermal Studies","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A stationary study solves the state in which time derivatives vanish, making it appropriate for equilibrium operating conditions. A time-dependent study advances from an initial condition and records how temperature, flow, and stored energy evolve.\n\nThe choice follows the question rather than a preference for shorter runs. A stationary model cannot report warm-up time or transient overshoot, while a time-dependent model may use a stationary solution